(1718348, 232697, 36628, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure I get the challenge relation...Technically the photo looks a little over exposed, toning down the highlights might help out alot, or decreasing the brightness and increasing contrast, the composition is a little too busy, all of the limbs of the tree make it almost impossible to pick out a particular element of the scene. The placement of the tree in the middle of the frame also detracts from the image becasue it doesnt leave the eye much room to wander to anything else in the picture. <br/> <br/>From what I can tell you were trying to compare the tower and the tree? If thats the case, you might have placed the tree on the left side of the frame and the tower on the right edge of the tree. That would increase the interest of the photo, and it would also take out alot of the dead space in the upper-left corner. Hope this helps some, let me know if you have any questions.</td>', 'I''m not sure I get the challenge relation...Technically the photo looks a little over exposed, toning down the highlights might help out alot, or decreasing the brightness and increasing contrast, the composition is a little too busy, all of the limbs of the tree make it almost impossible to pick out a particular element of the scene. The placement of the tree in the middle of the frame also detracts from the image becasue it doesnt leave the eye much room to wander to anything else in the picture.  From what I can tell you were trying to compare the tower and the tree? If thats the case, you might have placed the tree on the left side of the frame and the tower on the right edge of the tree. That would increase the interest of the photo, and it would also take out alot of the dead space in the upper-left corner. Hope this helps some, let me know if you have any questions.', '2005-09-18 11:15:16.000000', NULL, 1),
