(1749730, 232340, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>This is great conspiracy image.  I love the idea, it is really great to see something like this! I would be curious to see the image in black and white like one of the voters had stated.  I also think the image may have scored a little better based on those lashes being in focus.  I am sure this way an extremely hard image to shot, and I can appreciate the thought and effort.  I personally like the blood shot lines being included in this photo.  I was watching Nip Tuck the other night and Christian has a photo like this minus the pyramid and it is just amazing. It is really interesting to see a photo like this after seeing that one.  I think you probably would have jumped to the top 20 with those lashes being focus, but great job on this shot.</td>', '*Critique Club* This is great conspiracy image.  I love the idea, it is really great to see something like this! I would be curious to see the image in black and white like one of the voters had stated.  I also think the image may have scored a little better based on those lashes being in focus.  I am sure this way an extremely hard image to shot, and I can appreciate the thought and effort.  I personally like the blood shot lines being included in this photo.  I was watching Nip Tuck the other night and Christian has a photo like this minus the pyramid and it is just amazing. It is really interesting to see a photo like this after seeing that one.  I think you probably would have jumped to the top 20 with those lashes being focus, but great job on this shot.', '2005-09-30 01:23:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(1749734, 232460, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Great job protecting the "anonymity." I love this shot, it is so cute for the challenge.  I am so glad to see you place in the top 20.  I am not sure if there is much or anything that could be improved. The background is great and allows the viewer to focus on the subject.  I love how beady the mice''s eyes look, just like a really conspiracy. The only tiny thing I could see which may have been impossible in a shot like this would be a little more focus on the fallers bottom.   My image blurs a little there, but that really is a minor thing.  Congrats on the challenge!</td>', '*Critique Club* Great job protecting the "anonymity." I love this shot, it is so cute for the challenge.  I am so glad to see you place in the top 20.  I am not sure if there is much or anything that could be improved. The background is great and allows the viewer to focus on the subject.  I love how beady the mice''s eyes look, just like a really conspiracy. The only tiny thing I could see which may have been impossible in a shot like this would be a little more focus on the fallers bottom.   My image blurs a little there, but that really is a minor thing.  Congrats on the challenge!', '2005-09-30 01:31:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(1749754, 232316, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>This is a prefect sinister image.  This really took some vision, and I think it was very well rewarded by the top 10 finish, congrats! My favorite part of this shot is the lighting, I am so glad you spent the time on it. What an awesome roommate you have, I am sure it won''t be the last time we see him. I also really like the fade to dark on the bottom. Overall this photo is just excellent.  Great job on nailing the theme.  I wish there was more I could say but good job!</td>', '*Critique Club* This is a prefect sinister image.  This really took some vision, and I think it was very well rewarded by the top 10 finish, congrats! My favorite part of this shot is the lighting, I am so glad you spent the time on it. What an awesome roommate you have, I am sure it won''t be the last time we see him. I also really like the fade to dark on the bottom. Overall this photo is just excellent.  Great job on nailing the theme.  I wish there was more I could say but good job!', '2005-09-30 01:42:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1749781, 232672, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Very cool perspective on the conspiracy theme.  I am very glad you went with the black and white on this image it really draws the subject out.  The placement of the horse and tilt of the ones head is so prefect.  I would like to see just a little more clarity in the picture.  I am really glad you also keep the third horse in the picture, I think cropping him out would have really hurt the conspiracy aspect.  I really like the flow of the image, you really feel like the wind is blowing.  I also really like that you left the bottom fence post in, I think it adds to the composition of the photo. The title is also very appropriate, good job!</td>', '*Critique Club* Very cool perspective on the conspiracy theme.  I am very glad you went with the black and white on this image it really draws the subject out.  The placement of the horse and tilt of the ones head is so prefect.  I would like to see just a little more clarity in the picture.  I am really glad you also keep the third horse in the picture, I think cropping him out would have really hurt the conspiracy aspect.  I really like the flow of the image, you really feel like the wind is blowing.  I also really like that you left the bottom fence post in, I think it adds to the composition of the photo. The title is also very appropriate, good job!', '2005-09-30 01:56:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1749791, 232653, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Ok the veggies are defiantly eerie, I am not sure if I get the conspiracy but there is defiantly something here.  The image is just creepy, maybe its the lighting.  Excellent job on the shot, it might be a touch over burned because on my screen there are some pink blotches on the tomatoes and potato.  I saw a comment about the carrot being to long but I think it fits just right into the image.  If I had taken the photo I may have cropped the roof a little if it didn''t make the image look to long.   I think you placed very well, I think if the conspiracy were much clearly it would have bumped you right up the ladder.  Good job on making even veggies look scary.</td>', '*Critique Club* Ok the veggies are defiantly eerie, I am not sure if I get the conspiracy but there is defiantly something here.  The image is just creepy, maybe its the lighting.  Excellent job on the shot, it might be a touch over burned because on my screen there are some pink blotches on the tomatoes and potato.  I saw a comment about the carrot being to long but I think it fits just right into the image.  If I had taken the photo I may have cropped the roof a little if it didn''t make the image look to long.   I think you placed very well, I think if the conspiracy were much clearly it would have bumped you right up the ladder.  Good job on making even veggies look scary.', '2005-09-30 02:09:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(1749823, 232577, 22970, '<td valign="top"><i>From the Critique Club</i> <br/> <br/>Hi,<br/>First off I have found on this site along with others that political and religious photographs tend not to score as high as other which if find a shame. I think no matter what statement is the photograph should be judged as a photograph. With that said the focus on you photograph is great on the hand and film rolls but very soft on the letter with in my opinion is the point of the conspiracy that you are trying to show in this photograph. That became a distraction to me. The photograph is pretty clean, thats a plus. I dont see any scratches, dust spots, stains, lens flare, etc. but do see some blue fringing around the right side film roll and top of paper. Your exposure and lighting is good. The colors are good but I cant help but wonder if maybe a black and white or duo-tone would of worked well with you photograph.<br/> <br/>You have good balance within your photograph but the arrangements of elements (paper) seem to split the picture up into two halfs causing my eyes to jump from one side to the other. The center of attention seems to be split between the paper and the hand with film and they are competing with each other because of the split feel of the picture and the bright colors on the left and toned down (almost B&amp;W) on the right. So in my opinion you had several distractions.<br/> <br/>You photograph really does not capture my attention and hold it the way its laid out and with the color scheme and does not have a wow factor to increase its value.  However it is provocative and makes one think and that counts a lot. I think another composition could of made your statement stronger. <br/> <br/>To sum up things you have a political/religious motivated picture that has a few distractions and does not really hold the voters eye. You did however use a usual objects portrayed in an unusual way giving your photograph creativity.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work and I hope you find this comment helpful.<br/></td>', 'From the Critique Club  Hi,First off I have found on this site along with others that political and religious photographs tend not to score as high as other which if find a shame. I think no matter what statement is the photograph should be judged as a photograph. With that said the focus on you photograph is great on the hand and film rolls but very soft on the letter with in my opinion is the point of the conspiracy that you are trying to show in this photograph. That became a distraction to me. The photograph is pretty clean, thats a plus. I dont see any scratches, dust spots, stains, lens flare, etc. but do see some blue fringing around the right side film roll and top of paper. Your exposure and lighting is good. The colors are good but I cant help but wonder if maybe a black and white or duo-tone would of worked well with you photograph. You have good balance within your photograph but the arrangements of elements (paper) seem to split the picture up into two halfs causing my eyes to jump from one side to the other. The center of attention seems to be split between the paper and the hand with film and they are competing with each other because of the split feel of the picture and the bright colors on the left and toned down (almost B&W) on the right. So in my opinion you had several distractions. You photograph really does not capture my attention and hold it the way its laid out and with the color scheme and does not have a wow factor to increase its value.  However it is provocative and makes one think and that counts a lot. I think another composition could of made your statement stronger.  To sum up things you have a political/religious motivated picture that has a few distractions and does not really hold the voters eye. You did however use a usual objects portrayed in an unusual way giving your photograph creativity. Keep up the good work and I hope you find this comment helpful.', '2005-09-30 02:47:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(1749872, 232031, 30364, '<td valign="top">Hi Steve, &amp; greetings from the Critique Club.<br/>Well, I don''t hail from your parts, so I am really just guessing that the conspiracy is that a $65 pack of oil ain''t really worth that much.  It''s a basic 10W-30 oil, so for 65 bucks that pack size had better be a few gallons! (and I''m guessing again ... it''s not).  Anyway, oil company conspiracies always appeal, so your idea is OK.  The photograph is pretty good; nice off-centre composition, sharp focus and good lighting all work well.  A tiny bit of light bounced back onto the label might have helped me read the pack size, so I''d be able to assess the extent of the rip-off that is the point of your image.  There''s not much to say beyond that; it''s a good if parochial idea (sort of like an "in" joke), and a respectable photograph.  Not exciting, but not dull either.</td>', 'Hi Steve, & greetings from the Critique Club.Well, I don''t hail from your parts, so I am really just guessing that the conspiracy is that a $65 pack of oil ain''t really worth that much.  It''s a basic 10W-30 oil, so for 65 bucks that pack size had better be a few gallons! (and I''m guessing again ... it''s not).  Anyway, oil company conspiracies always appeal, so your idea is OK.  The photograph is pretty good; nice off-centre composition, sharp focus and good lighting all work well.  A tiny bit of light bounced back onto the label might have helped me read the pack size, so I''d be able to assess the extent of the rip-off that is the point of your image.  There''s not much to say beyond that; it''s a good if parochial idea (sort of like an "in" joke), and a respectable photograph.  Not exciting, but not dull either.', '2005-09-30 04:18:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(1755164, 232284, 16406, '<td valign="top">thank you all... I was really sad about seeing someone cared more about the title than the photo, in fact I hate put titles cause they can help but aren''t part of the work....<br/>those letters were just the initial of the names of these friends who gentle posed for me... we were out at night after a great steak it was really dark... so my 1.8F and 1600iso was not enough, and noise reduction did the rest for the plastic look :) I''m happy for my top 20 of course</td>', 'thank you all... I was really sad about seeing someone cared more about the title than the photo, in fact I hate put titles cause they can help but aren''t part of the work....those letters were just the initial of the names of these friends who gentle posed for me... we were out at night after a great steak it was really dark... so my 1.8F and 1600iso was not enough, and noise reduction did the rest for the plastic look :) I''m happy for my top 20 of course', '2005-10-03 05:31:26.000000', NULL, 0),
